## A1: tried, measured, and the map kept (ruling §1)
I built A1 (walk the parent chain at each rule entry, no map) and timed it against the map on the same at-bound shapes, three fresh runs each:

| shape | map (ms) | A1 walk (ms) | change |
|---|---|---|---|
| parens 908 | 84 | 150 | +79% |
| not 8178 | 710 | 790 | +11% |
| ternary 8178 | 2,900 | 6,040 | +110% |
| bs-ternary 8178 | 3,290 | 7,350 | +123% |
| lambda 4089 | 542 | 638 | +18% |
| comp-for 4085 | 1,435 | 2,430 | +69% |
| indent 2045 | 832 | 1,442 | +73% |
| call 408 | 338 | 370 | +9% |

Seven shapes are more than 10% slower, so as §1 prescribes the map stays. The comments and docs carry the A1 soundness wording (the chain length equals the live activations), state that `exitRule` is not virtual and that there are no labelled alternatives, and record why the map was kept.

